## CS50x 2024 - Introduction to Computer Science

Completed Harvard's CS50x 2024 course, covering 10 weeks of introductory computer science topics



---
Course Structure & Covered Topics

Week 0: Scratch - Visual programming concepts and basic logic flow.

Week 1: C - Syntax, data types, conditionals, and loops.

Week 2: Arrays - Command-line arguments, strings, and basic cryptography concepts.

Week 3: Algorithms - Linear search, binary search, and basic sorting algorithms (Bubble, Selection, Merge).

Week 4: Memory - Pointers, memory allocation, and pointers manipulation.

Week 5: Data Structures - Linked lists, queues, stacks, trees, and hash tables.

Week 6: Python - Rewriting C programs in Python to compare syntax and abstraction.

Week 7: SQL - Relational databases, SQL queries, indexing, and data filtering.

Week 8: HTML, CSS, JavaScript - Basics of web development and frontend interaction.

Week 9: Flask - Building basic web apps using Python and HTML forms.

Week 10: Cybersecurity - Overview of basic security concepts, threats, and privacy.
